#
# The C compiler script/remote-gate builds with: the gcc on PATH, with
# what CI's GCC 11 needs no help with. GCC 15 reports -Warray-bounds in
# Ruby 4.0's headers, and GCC 13 and 15 -Wmaybe-uninitialized in
# libstdc++'s <regex> under ASan, which -Werror makes fatal; both vectorize
# libmodplug into a dependency on libmvec, which CI's build does not
# link. The flags are here rather than in CFLAGS, which clang-tidy would
# read back from compile_commands.json.
exec gcc -Wno-error=array-bounds -Wno-error=maybe-uninitialized -fno-tree-vectorize "$@"
